<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hanoi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hanoi is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> on the Red River, the historic centre of Vietnamese states. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> it became the seat of the governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">French Indochina</a>. It was the administrative hub from which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> governed its territories in South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hanoi.jpg" alt="Hanoi" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quangnlnhe182394 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hanoi_skyline_with_Ba_Vi_Mountain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
